From: Deividas Nastajus <16858119+dns54@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 18:45:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 24/29] security/tpm/tss/tcg-2.0: Reject PCR selections larger
 than pcrSelect[]

The TPM_CAP_PCRS response gives each bank's sizeofSelect, which
tlcl2_get_capability_pcrs() uses to memcpy() pcrSelect[] into a
caller's struct, and the TPM 2.0 log code then scans that many bytes.
pcrSelect[] holds PCR_SELECT_MAX (3) bytes, enough for the 24 PCRs of
a PC Client TPM, but the value comes from the TPM unchecked: a faulty
TPM, or a device on the LPC bus pretending to be one, can make
coreboot write up to 252 bytes past the array on the stack.

Fail the unmarshalling when sizeofSelect doesn't fit, as is already
done when there are more banks than pcrSelections[] holds.

Signed-off-by: Deividas Nastajus <16858119+dns54@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 src/security/tpm/tss/tcg-2.0/tss_marshaling.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/security/tpm/tss/tcg-2.0/tss_marshaling.c b/src/security/tpm/tss/tcg-2.0/tss_marshaling.c
index 121d7bb1d9..a65c1fd57a 100644
--- a/src/security/tpm/tss/tcg-2.0/tss_marshaling.c
+++ b/src/security/tpm/tss/tcg-2.0/tss_marshaling.c
@@ -498,6 +498,9 @@ static int unmarshal_get_capability(struct ibuf *ib,
 			TPMS_PCR_SELECTION *pp =
 				&gcr->cd.data.assignedPCR.pcrSelections[i];
 			rc |= ibuf_read(ib, pp, sizeof(TPMS_PCR_SELECTION));
+			/* Callers copy and scan sizeofSelect bytes of pcrSelect[] */
+			if (pp->sizeofSelect > ARRAY_SIZE(pp->pcrSelect))
+				return -1;
 		}
 		break;
 	default:
